{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VladKochetov007/WunderFunder/pulls/61","id":5155242277,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUw2uXs8AAAABM0bBJQ","html_url":"https://github.com/VladKochetov007/WunderFunder/pull/61","diff_url":"https://github.com/VladKochetov007/WunderFunder/pull/61.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/VladKochetov007/WunderFunder/pull/61.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VladKochetov007/WunderFunder/issues/61","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VladKochetov007/WunderFunder/pulls/61/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VladKochetov007/WunderFunder/pulls/61/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VladKochetov007/WunderFunder/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VladKochetov007/WunderFunder/issues/61/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VladKochetov007/WunderFunder/statuses/a6456b44304b79ac149a9c2b70cc036fcaf6e079","number":61,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[Experiment] L4 teacher capacity and student transfer","user":{"login":"SemyonEpanov","id":142408295,"node_id":"U_kgDOCHz6Zw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142408295?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SemyonEpanov","html_url":"https://github.com/SemyonEpanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SemyonEpanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SemyonEpanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SemyonEpanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SemyonEpanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SemyonEpanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SemyonEpanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SemyonEpanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SemyonEpanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SemyonEpanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# E-L4-TEACHER-CAPACITY-20261104: fresh teacher capacity and measured student transfer\n\n1. **Status, lineage and owner.** Authorized12-fit continuation after PR60, owned by SemyonEpanov. All6 native-GRU scientific fits completed4epochs;2 Transformer fits are running;4 students have a separately admitted continuation and independent cache-review gate. Resource profiles are counted separately. GRU source27e605aa488651a3ab6cd38d3a1965075c24760f; Transformer sourceffebdbdc573e4494e0b53bd661c544ecc490b3df. See CONTRACT_R1.json, receiving bindings and reviews/.\n\n2. **Why it should work.** PR60 warm-target/loss variations yielded no useful improvement. Test fresh teacher capacity and architecture diversity, then whether each fixed family improves the same compact W18 student. A stronger teacher alone is insufficient; failure of student or fixed-mixture benefit falsifies the practical transfer claim.\n\n3. **Compute advantage.** Eight existing L4 GPUs run independent scratch teachers concurrently. Larger GRUs and a causal Transformer buy fitting capacity and diversity while the deployable student remains GRU256x2. No new rental, invented scaling law, or public-score forecast.\n\n4. **Frozen comparison.** GRU256x2 control,384x2 and512x1, each seeds1001/1002,4epochs/fixed zero-basedep3; event211, strict FP32, WMSE and native next/structural auxiliaries .3, B32/C1000, gatewise Muon plus AdamW, LR1e-3/OneCycle5%warmup. Strict-FP32 Muon is an explicit adaptation from legacy BF16 Newton-Schulz work. Transformer d384/L8/H8/window1024/FFN1536, AdamW3e-4/warmup-cosine, selectedB32/accum1/C1024 with efficient FP32 attention and activation checkpointing disabled;4epochs/fixedep3. All resource changes preceded its fitting; original mathB8/accum4 projected15.4h, selected preset8.4h training plus evaluation. Exact commands/configs/source/data bind every actual profile and fit.\n\n5. **Bounded fitting panel.** Exactly8newteacherfits plus4newstudentfits;12total, not12perarm. The prospective small-screen default is superseded by the user's accepted exact allocation. Two seeds per architecture; no fabricated chronological folds. Reuse PR60 exact eligible W18 controls. Students: two fixed teacher families x seeds1001/1002,2epochs/fixedep1, same clean FBCseed5 initializer and W18 alpha.7/family.1/AdamW1e-4/B16/C2000. New main target is .8*T_old+.2*.8125*mean(clip(new_family_prediction,-2,2)); original four auxiliary family arrays remain unchanged. Wide family contains all4wide-GRU teachers; Transformer family both Transformer teachers, all fixedep3.\n\n6. **Validation and uncertainty.** Official train10325 -> full official valid1873sequences/3528273scoredrows. Metric global_wp_clip2_v1 on is_scored and row>=99. Preserve seed-wise endpoints and fixed .9TL3+.1candidate mixtures. Previously inspected valid is exposed development, not independent confirmation. Two seeds cannot establish reliable training variability or significance.\n\n7. **Leakage and coverage.** Split SHA0c4de3a253d23b3a5d5ca73b7aeb7fcae2b974673e4f9ec51e94e593c59d114c. Teachers start fresh; transforms/normalizers fit only fitting train members; validation excluded from all teacher/initializer/cache ancestry. Whole sequences and causal resets are mandatory. Shuffled seq_ix provides no chronology. GALAM exact reconstruction and all-corpus submission weights are not used.\n\n8. **Decision-changing result.** Useful singleton delta is .001; useful fixed-blend delta .0005 over its anchor. These are allocation thresholds, not promised improvements. Teacher-only gain without student benefit does not promote the endpoint. Negative, partial and failed runs remain in the record.\n\n9. **How to run.** Existing node lc-epanov_s@10.61.10.209, runtime /data2/lc-epanov_s/tabdata/runtime/l4-teacher-capacity-20261104-r1, one GPU per teacher. Source/checkpoint/recipe/data/environment bound in receiving receipts. Native runner has separate profile/fit phases and independently reviewed admission. Transformer reuses train_sequence.py with its mandatory exact-profile gate. Twelve-hour shared limit from first profile,45min collection reserve,64CPUcores/400GiB owned RAM,6.5GBnewoutputcap/3GBfreefloor. Detached workers survive SSH disconnect; no foreign-process actions or blind retries.\n\n   The streamed stage-2 target implementation and commands are in [STAGE2_HANDOFF_R1.md](STAGE2_HANDOFF_R1.md); its full-index mapping correction and revised disk bound are in [STAGE2_HANDOFF_R2.md](STAGE2_HANDOFF_R2.md).\n\n10. **Evidence to return.** Per-cell argv/source/config/split/parents; epoch checkpoints; train/control/official-valid loss and score curves; LR/preclip gradients/nonfinite/skipped updates; CPU/RAM/VRAM/utilization; fixed-epoch compact prediction exports and canonical grades. Publish separate evidence/weight artifacts with SHA256 and receiving receipts; preserve failed R1 admission (no scientific updates) and its diagnosed missing-field repair.\n\n11. **Results and trace.** [Completed GRU report and graphs](RESULTS_GRU_20261104_R1.md): fixedep3 WP means control .68513454,384x2 .68221578,512x1 .68190412. Larger teachers are worse than matched controls. All6 best-observed checkpoints areep2 and remain distinct from the primary fixed endpoint. An earlier conversational +.003 gain paragraph was a terminal-transcription error; it is withdrawn and corrected from JSON. GRU profiles each completed1360finite updates; selected TF profiles each completed50. [Stage2R2](STAGE2_HANDOFF_R2.md) maps10607 full-source prediction groups to10325 fitting groups, excluding282. Pre-fit initialization/launcher/panel-adapter failures are preserved; no learned fit was rerun for those repairs. Transformer/student endpoints and leaderboard impact remain pending.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T13:39:40Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T01:04:07Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"b57c4925